X:4
T:Mairi's Wedding
C:John Roderick Bannerman 1934 
N:Originally written in Gaelic by John Roderick Bannerman (1865 - 1938) for Mary C. MacNiven (1905 - 1997) on the occasion of her winning the gold medal at the National Mod in 1934. In 1959, James B. Cosh devised a Scottish country dance to the tune, which is 40 bars, in reel time.
